Quick safety note: please avoid posting your full SSN or other sensitive numbers in chat. I see you supplied a masked/partial value — I won’t store it — but try not to paste SSNs here going forward.

Now, to your question: I need one quick clarification to give a precise answer — which country’s visa are you applying for (or which country will you be visiting)? Visa/passport validity rules differ by country.

General guidance (what most countries require)
- Rule of thumb: many countries require your passport to be valid for at least six months beyond your intended date of entry or beyond your planned date of exit/return. If your passport will expire within that six‑month window, you should renew it before applying for a six‑month visa or traveling.
- Some countries require only 3 months beyond your planned departure (e.g., many Schengen countries), while others require validity for the entire duration of stay (e.g., UK) or six months (common). Airlines may also refuse boarding if your passport doesn’t meet the destination’s entry rules.
- If your visa starts on your entry date and allows a six‑month stay, make sure your passport expiry is later than the end of that six‑month period (and later than any extra buffer the destination requires).

Concrete example
- If you plan to enter Country X on July 1 and your visa allows a six‑month stay (so you could exit as late as January 1), and Country X requires 6 months’ validity after entry, your passport should be valid at least through January 1 — ideally through the end of January 1 plus whatever buffer the embassy specifies.

What I can do for you
- If you tell me:
  1) which country the visa is for, and
  2) your passport expiry date (and/or intended entry and exit dates),
I’ll check the typical requirement and tell you whether the expiry is too close and whether you should renew before applying. I can also:
  - Look up the embassy page requirement for that country, or
  - Draft an email to the passport agency or the embassy if you want to ask for clarification or request expedited renewal.

Tell me the country and your passport expiry (or travel dates) and I’ll calculate and advise.

